# New calculator checklist

When adding a new calculator to AFL, complete ALL of these steps:

## Required files

1. **`src/lib/tool-registry.ts`** — Add tool entry with `id`, `title`, `description`, `interpretationMethod`, `relatedTools`, `relatedEditorial`, `status: "live"`
2. **`src/app/[locale]/{slug}/page.tsx`** — Calculator page using `CalculatorShell` + form + `FAQSection` + `RelatedTools`
3. **`src/app/[locale]/{slug}/layout.tsx`** — Metadata via `toolMetadata()` from `src/lib/seo.ts`
4. **`messages/en/tools.json`** — Full i18n copy (intro, sections, FAQ items) — do NOT hardcode English in the component

## Content requirements

- Server-rendered educational intro paragraph (visible before interaction)
- 3-4 FAQ items passed to `FAQSection` (auto-emits FAQPage JSON-LD)
- Related tools links (3 related calculators)
- Results must include interpretive text, not just numbers/charts

## Also update

- `src/i18n/routing.ts` — Add pathname for the new route
- `src/app/sitemap.ts` — Tool auto-included via `getSitemapTools()` if `status: "live"`
- `src/i18n/translated-routes.ts` — Add for published locales (es, pt) when translations exist
- `messages/es/tools.json` and `messages/pt/tools.json` — Add translations
- `src/lib/editorial-content.ts` — Consider creating a matching guide article
- Footer and homepage — Add link if it's a primary calculator

## Anti-patterns

- Do NOT create a calculator with only a form and no server-rendered text
- Do NOT hardcode English strings — use `useTranslations` from next-intl
- Do NOT skip the FAQSection — every calculator needs FAQ rich results
